WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight i
an Emmy and Tony Award-winning

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
actress you know from her work
on "The Good Fight,"

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Good Wife," and
the "Mamma Mia!" movies.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
She is hosting the
Stage &amp; Screen auction

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
benefiting The Actors Fund
and presented by

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:16.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
Doyle Auctioneers &amp; Appraisers
on Wednesday, April 28th.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back
to the show now --

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
Christine, there's
no audience here,

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you are a star
and I would like you

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:25.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
to walk out like you're
receiving a standing ovation

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.659 line:92%
from a full Broadway theater

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome
Christine Baranski.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.196 size:88% position:44% line:92%
[ Majestic music plays ]

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light applause ]

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.468 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughing ]

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:38.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
They know!
They love you!

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.341 line:92%
[ Chuckling ] They love you.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
Oh, my God.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't realize she had
a second level down.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.783 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
Welcome.
I'm so sorry

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't be a gentleman
and take your hand

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.889
and do all the things
that we can do in simpler times.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.458 size:78% position:39%
-You know that bow --
when is the last time

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:00.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
you saw anybody bow?
-You're right.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's no performers bowin
anymore.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No one is bowing,
and yet there's

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:07.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
a bit of a light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the very fact
that right now

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
Christine Baranski
is in Midtown Manhattan

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a good sign.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a good sign,
don't you think?

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:14.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a good sign.
And we've got to bring

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
Midtown back, you know,
in the bright lights, don't we

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
My God.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's been a long time.
Remember back when we said

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:26.019
"Oh, my God, they're shuttin
down production for two weeks"

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:26.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-Wow.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it was, like, summe
and then, "Oh,

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:31.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'll be back in the fall,
and here we are.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:32.959 line:92%
-Well, the other thing was

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
it just didn't even seem
feasible

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.329 size:88% position:44%
that you could shut down
Broadway for two weeks,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, as you know,
for someone who's involved

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a show like that, there's
so many people involved.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.838 size:88% position:44%
-There's so many people.
It is a huge community.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've discovered this,
working with the Actors Fund

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:53.546
that the Actors Fund -- we'r
doing this auction for them --

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:57.884 size:84% position:42%
it helps so many people
and not just actors.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.653 size:84% position:42%
It's everybody involved
in the performing arts.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.656 size:81% position:41%
So, if you think about
who those people are

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that they
have not been working --

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're talking
stage hands, designers,

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.196 size:84% position:42% line:92%
hair and makeup people,

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
the people
that take the tickets,

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
all of the performers --
musicians, singers, dancers --

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, these peopl
have been home.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:21.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've not been able
to go and do what they do.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:26.212
And you know,
the financial support is just --

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
been, you know,
a terrible issue for them.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
theater actors and performer

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
usually work
paycheck to paycheck,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.455 size:88% position:44%
or they don't have big,
you know, bank accounts.

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For anybody who's been
backstage at a Broadway show

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:41.060
or even in the dressing room
of a star of a Broadway show

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
you realize --
-The dressing rooms

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:46.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
are so small, and
you usually have to climb

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:48.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
many stairs to get
to your dressing room.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you're, you know,
a chorus member,

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're scrunched in
with a lot of other people

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the basement
or all the way up.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.811
And, no, their life is hard,
and it's eight shows a week.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not a lot of money,
but to shut it all down

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:06.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to have Broadway be dark -
and not just Broadway

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
but all over the country,
regional theaters,

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:11.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
concert halls --
all of the performing arts

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
have been affected.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the Actors Fund
has been amazing.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a huge
national organization,

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:24.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think it's given away $2
million for about 16,000 -

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
$22 million for
16,000 people so far.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's everything
from groceries

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:34.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
and helping with rent
and healthcare and insurance

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:37.083 line:92%
and mental health support.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:41.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been an enormous lifeline
to people.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.890
-And so this auction is,
obviously, to raise money

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.758 size:81% position:41%
for the Actors Fund.
and you're hosting it.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you the actual auctioneer?
-Oh, my gosh, no.

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not hosting it,
and, God help me, no,

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not the auctioneer.
It was my idea last spring

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I came out of the closet,
meaning my own closet,

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
thinking "Gee,
two weeks off from work?

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:03.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why not clean some closets?"
And like so many people,

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Okay, this is
an opportunity

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.247 size:78% position:39%
to get rid of stuff."
And I realized I had

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
these beautiful
hand-beaded gowns

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:14.420
and, you know, that I'd worn
for award shows or big events,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.691
and I was holding on to them
for, well, sentimental reasons

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they were taking up space.
And I thought, "you know,

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:24.197
if I gave them away now,
maybe to an auction house

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
or something,
I could make some money."

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.668
And then I thought, "I've go
a whole lot of girlfriends

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of them
that go by only one name,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
who probably have
bigger closets than me

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.876 line:92%
and really some fabulous stuff."

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:37.877 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So I started e-mailing,

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:40.813
and then I said, "Why don't we
do this for the Actors Fund.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:45.985
So, it was Meryl, then it wa
my new girlfriend, Dolly Parton,

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:47.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
with whom I did
a Christmas movie.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's the most generou
woman in the world.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:53.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, of course, she is not only
donating a gown

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
but her mannequin.
-Really?

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Her mannequin, which I want t
bid on the mannequins.

00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:00.533
Be like a piece of sculpture
in your living room, right

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.567 line:92%
-[ Laughing ] Absolutely, yeah

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.370
-And then we've got Cher,
and then we've got Bette.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we've got
all the Broadway divas.

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've got Patty LuPone and
Bernadette Peters

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Audra McDonald,
and you know, all of them.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.845 line:92%
They all said yes immediately.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I thought,
"Well, what about the guys?"

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:19.218
So we've got Hugh Jackman giving
his Wolverine leather jacket

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.920 line:92%
from, you know, his movie,

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:24.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we've got Steve Martin
an autographed banjo.

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:28.261
And I even had the guts,
because I've been backstag

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
with him a few times,
to get in touch

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:34.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Bruce Springsteen,
who is donating his boots,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
a T-shirt, and jeans.
-Wow!

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've just got a whole list.
I mean, we've got

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:46.112
the most amazing -- we've go
Stephen Sondheim wrote out

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first eight bars of
"Broadway baby"

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
and signed it,
and that's framed.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:56.889
So, that to me was, like, th
most incredible contribution

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:59.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Andrew Lloyd Webber
is donating

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:03.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little musical monkey
that was on the set

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the original production
of "Phantom" in London,

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:12.572
and he will personally escort,
whomever bids on his item --

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:15.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
he will personally escort them
into the theater

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:18.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the night
"Phantom of the Opera" reopens

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
That is quite an escort.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then we've got Judy Craymer
producer of "Mamma Mia!"

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:28.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
is donating
my character, Tanya's,

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:33.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
final curtain-call outfit.
And Lorne Michaels --

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:35.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
I reached out to Lorne
and I said,

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:39.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Lorne, can you just get m
Tina Fey's e-mail?"

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:42.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, of course,
Tina Fey has contributed.

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:47.840
And Lorne said, "Yeah, I hav
a rather big closet from 'SNL.'"

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we've got RuPaul's
opening-monologue outfit,

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:54.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have
Timothée Chalamet's costum

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:56.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he played Harry Style
on "SNL."

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:58.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
I thought he was gonna give yo

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
stuff from the Lorne Michael
personal closet...

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-...which I'm pretty sure is

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:05.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
just like, "I have,
like, a teal polo."

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:09.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"My summer polo."

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:13.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Anyway, does any of this
appeal to you?

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:15.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it appeals to me
a great deal.

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.937
-I mean, there's Bryan Cranston,
Alan Cumming,

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:20.606
Victor Garber, John Lithgow,
and then all of these great,

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:25.011
you know, theater actresses --
Laurie Metcalf, Cherry Jones

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:28.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
Andrea Martin, Debra Monk.
It's been tremendous.

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:33.519
People, performers get wha
other performers go through,

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:36.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
and anyone who's done a show
knows how hard it is.

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, the people
above the title,

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:42.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're not what really make u
the Broadway community.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:46.098
The Broadway community are
those hardworking people,

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:46.999 line:92%
particularly the young people.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:50.503
-I do have a few more question
about that wonderful community

00:07:50.503 --> 00:07:53.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back
with more Christine Baranski

